            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <instructions>Use bigger shells made with whole wheat flour. Fill with potatoes and chickpeas. Use very spicy and savory pani. Often includes shredded hard boiled eggs.</instructions>
        <rdfs:comment>Fuchka is a beloved South Asian street food consisting of small, crispy, hollow dough balls stuffed with a savory, spicy mixture and dipped in tangy tamarind water. It is the Bengali variation of the popular pani puri or golgappa</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Fuchka</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


