            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://example.org/southasianstreetfood#hasPrepTime"/>
                <owl:minQualifiedCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">60</owl:minQualifiedCardinality>
                <owl:onDataRange rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <instructions>Crack open a crispy fried puri (hollow ball) and stuff with seasoned boiled potatoes 
and chickpeas. Fill to the brim with mint based spiced water (pani) and eat 
immediately in one mouthful.</instructions>
        <rdfs:comment>Gol Gappay (also known as pani puri) is a popular, bite-sized South Asian street food. It consists of a hollow, crispy-fried shell (puri) filled with a mixture of boiled potatoes, chickpeas, and spices, which is then dipped into flavored, tangy water (usually mint or tamarind) and eaten in one whole bite.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Gol Gappay</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


