                <owl:onDataRange rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <instructions>Crack open a crispy fried puri (hollow ball) and stuff with seasoned boiled potatoes 
and chickpeas. Fill to the brim with tangy spiced tamarind water (pani) and eat 
immediately in one mouthful.</instructions>
        <rdfs:comment>Pani Puri is a popular, bite-sized Indian street food. It consists of a crispy, hollow fried dough ball (puri) stuffed with a mixture of potatoes and chickpeas, then filled to the brim with a tangy, spicy, and sweet flavored water (pani), and eaten in a single mouthful.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Pani Puri</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


